    "result_text": "Full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nChanged the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` with a per-city sequence.\n\n**`AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 the one place the code is minted:\n- `CITY3` = upper-cased first 3 letters of the owner's city\n- `LAST3` = upper-cased first 3 letters of the last name\n- `NNNN` = per-city 4-digit sequence, computed as one more than the owners already in that same city (filtering `findAll()` by city, case-insensitive), replacing the old global count\n- Format is now `\"%s-%s-%04d\"` \u2192 e.g. `LON-SMI-0007`\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 `membershipNumber` embeds the `customerCode` (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`), so it automatically rebuilds on the new format (e.g. `LON-SMI-0007-M26`). I only updated the Javadoc example to match; no logic change was needed since it derives directly from the code.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix` (asserting `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`) passes, as does the full suite.",
