        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is coherent, additive, and idiomatic for this codebase.\n\n- Logic is in the right unit: the customerCode format lives entirely in `AssignOwnerCustomerCode.service`, the one function wired for that step in `owners.POST.yml`. No logic leaked into the mapper or model.\n- The one derived value, `membershipNumber`, is built by composition (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`), so it automatically inherits the new city prefix \u2014 no code change was needed there, only the javadoc example, which was correctly updated to `LON-SMI-0007-M26`. Nothing else in the tree derives from `customerCode`.\n- Javadoc on `AssignOwnerCustomerCode` was updated to match the new behavior (per-city sequence, CITY3 component), so the class stays self-documenting.\n- No class or method is turning into a catch-all; the method stayed small and single-purpose.\n\nMinor, not blocking: `city3` and `last3` repeat the same `substring(0, Math.min(3, x.length())).toUpperCase()` idiom, which could be a tiny private helper. At two lines inside one short method it reads fine as-is, so this is a judgment call rather than a structural defect."
